course: dictionary
lesson: 13003
title: Extensively: widely and in detail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Extensively is an adverb. It tells you how far, how much or how thoroughly something happens. Think of it as big and wide: something done extensively is done over a large area or in many places.
explain: «The flood extensively damaged the town.» The clues are flood, damaged and town. A flood can wreck many houses across a wide area, so extensively means widely, over a large area.
explain: «She has travelled extensively.» Here it means she has been to many different places. Try the swap test: «She has travelled a lot» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Extensively can also mean in great detail and thoroughly. «The doctor extensively checked the patient» means every test was done carefully, one part at a time. Ask yourself: is it a big area, many places, or a very careful job? Then swap in a simpler word to check.
fact: Extensively is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens, such as how it was damaged or how it was studied.
fact: «Extensively» means a lot, widely, or over a large area or many places.
fact: «Extensively» can also mean in great detail and thoroughly.
fact: «Extensively damaged» means damaged over a large area.
fact: Its other forms are more extensively and most extensively.
exercise: «The flood extensively damaged the town.» What does extensively mean here? | Quietly and slowly | Without any care | *Over a large area | Only just
exercise: «She has travelled extensively.» What does it mean? | She has never left home | She has travelled by bus only | Very fast | *To many different places
exercise: «The doctor extensively checked the patient, every test and every part.» What does extensively suggest? | Without any care | In a sad way | Briefly and quickly | *In great detail and thoroughly
test: The team searched extensively for the lost dog. What does extensively mean here? | Without looking anywhere | *Over a wide area and very thoroughly | Only for one minute | Happily and loudly
test: «Many scientists have studied the disease extensively.» What does extensively suggest? | It was studied for a very short time | *A lot of work was done on it, in detail | The disease was only looked at once | The scientists were bored
exam: «The news spread extensively across the country.» Which word could replace extensively? | Slowly | *Widely | Quietly | Sadly
